498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (   If you thought your family's Thanksgiving traditions were elaborate, Pongal has you beat. Southern Indians, the Tamil, thank the Sun god, nature, and everyone and every animal who supports agriculture by hosting a four-day festival.    They observe it during the Tamil month Thai, which typically falls around January, but since it's based on the solar calendar it can vary. According to Business Insider, 'Pongal,' which translates to "overflowing" is a traditional dish made with milk, ghee, and rice. The Tamil culture regards it as a symbol of prosperity associated with abundance and affluence. During this festival of harvest, families share elaborate meals together, give thanks, dance, and say prayers.)
/E (   If you thought your family's Thanksgiving traditions were elaborate, Pongal has you beat. Southern Indians, the Tamil, thank the Sun god, nature, and everyone and every animal who supports agriculture by hosting a four-day festival.    They observe it during the Tamil month Thai, which typically falls around January, but since it's based on the solar calendar it can vary. According to Business Insider, 'Pongal,' which translates to "overflowing" is a traditional dish made with milk, ghee, and rice. The Tamil culture regards it as a symbol of prosperity associated with abundance and affluence. During this festival of harvest, families share elaborate meals together, give thanks, dance, and say prayers.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
