505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (    After suffering through a time of famine in the 16th century, the Ga people were finally blessed with rain to grow their crops and celebrated with a feast. This grew into a tradition known as the Homowo Festival. Homwow, which means "hooting at hunger" in the Ga language, stretches over three months from May until August. Traditional dances, singing, and street parades take place during this time. Of course, food is featured throughout including palm nut fish soup, yams, and a corn powder dish.)
/E (    After suffering through a time of famine in the 16th century, the Ga people were finally blessed with rain to grow their crops and celebrated with a feast. This grew into a tradition known as the Homowo Festival. Homwow, which means "hooting at hunger" in the Ga language, stretches over three months from May until August. Traditional dances, singing, and street parades take place during this time. Of course, food is featured throughout including palm nut fish soup, yams, and a corn powder dish.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [17]
>>
